  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, preferring the lottery with a greater probability mass on the favorable outcome (i.e., more left-skewed). However, in this case, the favorable outcome (non-zero amount) has a higher probability in A (0.2%) than in B (0.1%). Therefore, A is more left-skewed in terms of probability mass on the positive outcome. The verbal report does not mention probability, outcome amounts, or skewness at all. Instead, it focuses on the duration of play and the emotional appeal of staying in the game. There is no reference to comparing the distribution of outcomes or to the concept of skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason — they used a different justification based on play duration and psychological engagement. The information considered (duration, interest in staying) does not match the relevant information for skewness. The justification also does not follow the rule of preferring greater left-skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
